cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DisCoolPy: district cooling network simulation on TESPy"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-21"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AnasAlgarei/discoolpy"
url: "https://discoolpy.readthedocs.io/"
abstract: >-
  DisCoolPy is an open-source Python framework for district cooling network
  simulation, built on TESPy. It models a network as a tree of street branches
  and resolves heat gain wherever it occurs: buried and exposed pipes from
  geometry and insulation, weather-driven building envelopes, and ambient-driven
  cold storage. Pipe conductances are handed to TESPy's native UA group, so each
  duty is solved simultaneously with the water temperatures rather than assumed.
  Pressure and energy degrees of freedom across the whole tree are checked as
  graphs before any component is built. A scenario is a single YAML file, and
  four commands define, check, run and report on it.
